Follow the current plan.md and AGENTS.md. The primary experience is a quote grid beside an OpenCode chat, with files and a prompt sent directly to the agent for database maintenance.

The only application is tokensql.workspace. Do not restore the removed parser/semantic-import/review/publish pipeline, relational legacy schema, Streamlit, or legacy migration commands. Start with an empty database; never auto-import test files or cleanup backups.

All project changes and tests run on the authorized remote server. Do not create local project copies, read handoff/private handoff documents, or alter shared coding/model services.

Use the workspace store for validated transactional quote writes and audit records. Preserve unrelated changes; clear real data only at the user's explicit request and keep a recoverable backup outside the project. Keep agent jobs asynchronous so the quote grid stays responsive.

Record actual test and deployment evidence in progress.md. Do not treat mock results as real model or browser acceptance.
